<title>REPUBLIC OF IRELAND: Independent Newspapers H1 profit up 28 pct.</title>
<headline>Independent Newspapers H1 profit up 28 pct.</headline>
<dateline>DUBLIN 1996-09-11</dateline>
<text>
<p>Six months to June 30, 1996</p>
<p>			   (million punts unless stated)</p>
<p> Shr (p), fully diluted 6.97		   vs 6.07</p>
<p> Dividend (pence)	 2.3		    vs 2.05</p>
<p> Pretax profit	    26.02		  vs 20.37</p>
<p> Turnover		   182.54		 vs 167.54</p>
<p>NOTE - Analysts forecast half-year pre-tax profits of around 24 million Irish pounds compared with 20.37 million in the first half last year.  </p>
<p> Operating result	 25.07		  vs 21.89</p>
<p> Interest		   0.94 credit	  vs 3.25 charge</p>
<p> Tax charge		 5.76		   vs 4.87</p>
<p> Net taxed		  20.26		  vs 15.49</p>
<p> Retained profit	  8.37		   vs 7.86</p>
<p> Pay date		   Nov 1</p>
<p>Div registration date  Sep 20 NOTE - Independent Newspapers Plc said the 15 percent increase in first-half operating profit reflected strong performances from all of its businesses.</p>
<p>-- Dublin Newsroom +353 1 676 9779</p>
</text>
